# Decimal addition with integer operands

Adds 1.20 and 5 in both operand orders to verify the integer is promoted
and the result stays an exact decimal, producing 6.20 either way.

>>> source
decimal_left: decimal = 1.20
integer_right: int = 5

// Verifies the Decimal/Int promotion with the decimal operand first.
decimal_plus_integer: decimal = decimal_left + integer_right
print(decimal_plus_integer)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
integer_plus_decimal: decimal = integer_right + decimal_left
print(integer_plus_decimal)

<<< stdout
6.20
6.20

<<< stderr
